This product's design is informed by the Astral `uv` project
(https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) and by konstin's Rust implementations of
PEP 440 and PEP 508. No source from those projects is incorporated at this
time; attribution for any incorporated material is added when that material
lands.

The version/ package is derived from rstudio/go-pep440-version, itself a fork of
aquasecurity/go-pep440-version (https://github.com/aquasecurity/go-pep440-version),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The distribution/ package is ported from rstudio/python-distribution-parser
(https://github.com/rstudio/python-distribution-parser), Copyright (c) 2024
Posit Software, PBC, originally MIT-licensed.

The tags/ package adapts platform-compatibility-tag algorithms (manylinux and
musllinux glibc/musl floor tables, macOS format lists, tag ordering) from
pypa/packaging (https://github.com/pypa/packaging), specifically
packaging/tags.py, packaging/_manylinux.py, and packaging/_musllinux.py,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; and from Astral's uv
(https://github.com/astral-sh/uv), specifically the uv-platform-tags crate,
dual-licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, or the MIT license.

The wheelname/ package adapts wheel-filename parsing from pypa/packaging
(https://github.com/pypa/packaging), specifically
packaging/utils.py's `parse_wheel_filename`, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0; and from Astral's uv (https://github.com/astral-sh/uv),
specifically the uv-distribution-filename crate, dual-licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, or the MIT license.
